{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And HaShem your Elohim will circumcise your heart.</b> The Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote that He will remove from them the foreskin of the heart, for desire and the other lusts are the foreskin of the heart, and one who desires and inclines toward lusts is called 'arel (uncircumcised),' as it is written (Jeremiah 9:25): ״וכל בית ישראל ערלי לב״ — and all the house of Israel are uncircumcised of heart. And whoever does not desire and does not lust is called 'mul lev (circumcised of heart).' Therefore He promised them, in the time when the heart will do by its nature what reason requires — for the era will return to what it was before the sin of man — and this is what Jeremiah said (ibid. 31): ״הנה ימים באים נאם ה' וכרתי את בית ישראל ואת בית יהודה ברית חדשה״ — 'Behold, days are coming, declares YHWH, when I will cut with the house of Israel and the house of Judah a new covenant'; ״לא כברית אשר כרתי״ — 'not like the covenant that I cut'; ״זאת הברית אשר אכרות את בית ישראל אחרי הימים ההם נתתי את תורתי בקרבם ועל לבם אכתבנה״ — 'this is the covenant that I will cut with the house of Israel after those days: I will give My Torah within them and on their heart I will write it.' And the writing of the Torah upon the heart is the nullification of the evil impulse and the removal of all lusts, which is the circumcision of the heart."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The verse citations 'שם לא' refer to Jeremiah 31, the chapter of the new covenant prophecy; rendered as 'ibid. 31' following the source's reference back to the book of Jeremiah cited in the preceding line."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:52:14.554316595Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}